<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="route-planner"
  xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <name>Lakeland Way — Peaks</name>
    <desc>138 peaks near the route. OS grid references converted to WGS84, each validated against SRTM 30m elevation; positions failing the height check were excluded.</desc>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="54.372438" lon="-3.368438">
    <ele>231.0</ele>
    <name>Muncaster Fell 231m</name>
    <desc>A 231m wooded ridge near the coast at the very start and end of the route. Detour: +3.7km, +171m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.418943" lon="-3.308340">
    <ele>535.0</ele>
    <name>Whin Rigg 535m</name>
    <desc>The 535m southern end of the Wast Water Screes, above deep gullies. Detour: +16.0km, +678m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.434254" lon="-3.219408">
    <ele>762.0</ele>
    <name>Slight Side 762m</name>
    <desc>The 762m southern outpost of Scafell, a rocky top on the long Eskdale approach. Detour: +11.6km, +948m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.432701" lon="-3.282570">
    <ele>609.0</ele>
    <name>Illgill Head 609m</name>
    <desc>A 609m fell forming the top of the Wast Water Screes, which fall 500m straight into the deepest lake in England. Grassy and gentle from behind, spectacular at the edge. Detour: +4.4km, +325m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.446770" lon="-3.225948">
    <ele>964.0</ele>
    <name>Scafell 964m</name>
    <desc>Scafell Pike&apos;s separate and quieter neighbour at 964m. The direct link across Mickledore is blocked by Broad Stand, a rock climb — the walkers&apos; ways round are Lord&apos;s Rake or the Foxes Tarn gully, both loose and both requiring care. Detour: +5.3km, +829m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.464213" lon="-3.277384">
    <ele>628.0</ele>
    <name>Yewbarrow 628m</name>
    <desc>A 628m ridge above Wasdale with steep ends at both extremities. Detour: +7.4km, +548m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.484413" lon="-3.321235">
    <ele>797.0</ele>
    <name>Haycock 797m</name>
    <desc>A 797m remote top on the western fells above Ennerdale. Detour: +13.6km, +1149m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.482536" lon="-3.243997">
    <ele>802.0</ele>
    <name>Kirk Fell 802m</name>
    <desc>An 802m fell between Great Gable and Pillar, with steep grass on the Wasdale side. Detour: +6.0km, +659m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.462990" lon="-3.221805">
    <ele>800.0</ele>
    <name>Lingmell 800m</name>
    <desc>An 800m shoulder of Scafell Pike with a tremendous view of the Gable and down Wasdale — often walked over without being noticed. Detour: +8.5km, +578m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.481889" lon="-3.219281">
    <ele>899.0</ele>
    <name>Great Gable 899m</name>
    <desc>The 899m fell on the Lake District National Park emblem, with the war memorial of the Fell and Rock Climbing Club on its summit rocks. Steep on every side; the usual line from Styhead is the Breast Route. Detour: +4.6km, +567m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.485546" lon="-3.213216">
    <ele>801.0</ele>
    <name>Green Gable 801m</name>
    <desc>An 801m top separated from Great Gable by Windy Gap, with the best close view of the parent fell. Detour: +4.5km, +447m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.476745" lon="-3.194435">
    <ele>632.0</ele>
    <name>Seathwaite Fell 632m</name>
    <desc>A 632m knobbly fell of small tarns above Sprinkling Tarn. Detour: +2.5km, +104m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.454098" lon="-3.212285">
    <ele>978.0</ele>
    <name>Scafell Pike 978m</name>
    <desc>England&apos;s highest ground at 978m. A boulder-strewn summit plateau with a huge cairn; cairned throughout but genuinely serious in mist, where the plateau defeats casual navigation. Usual approach from the route is via Lingmell Col. Detour: +5.9km, +474m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.465065" lon="-3.194095">
    <ele>910.0</ele>
    <name>Great End 910m</name>
    <desc>The 910m northern buttress of the Scafell massif, with deep gullies holding snow late. Easily reached from Esk Hause and often missed by people hurrying to the Pike. Detour: +3.6km, +273m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.466099" lon="-3.180239">
    <ele>785.0</ele>
    <name>Allen Crags 785m</name>
    <desc>A 785m top on the Esk Hause crossing, an easy addition to a Scafell day. Detour: +0.6km, +52m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.457129" lon="-3.178438">
    <ele>885.0</ele>
    <name>Esk Pike 885m</name>
    <desc>An 885m rocky top between Bowfell and Great End, on the Esk Hause crossing. Detour: +3.6km, +287m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.447366" lon="-3.165820">
    <ele>902.0</ele>
    <name>Bowfell 902m</name>
    <desc>A 902m pyramid at the head of Langdale with a genuinely rocky top and the Great Slab on its flank. The Band gives a long but never technical ascent. Detour: +3.1km, +336m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.433947" lon="-3.159272">
    <ele>859.0</ele>
    <name>Crinkle Crags 859m</name>
    <desc>A 859m switchback of five distinct tops. The Bad Step on the second crinkle is a short awkward scramble — it can be bypassed on the west. Confusing ground in cloud. Detour: +7.0km, +647m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.457309" lon="-3.159932">
    <ele>651.0</ele>
    <name>Rossett Pike 651m</name>
    <desc>A 651m top above Rossett Gill and Angle Tarn at the head of Langdale. Detour: +1.4km, +79m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.427978" lon="-3.125191">
    <ele>705.0</ele>
    <name>Pike o’ Blisco 705m</name>
    <desc>A 705m top with two rocky summits and an outstanding view of the Crinkles. Detour: +14.9km, +1026m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.456888" lon="-3.108992">
    <ele>736.0</ele>
    <name>Harrison Stickle 736m</name>
    <desc>The highest of the Langdale Pikes at 736m, an abrupt rocky top with the whole valley beneath it. Detour: +5.1km, +313m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.457830" lon="-3.110693">
    <ele>700.0</ele>
    <name>Pavey Ark 700m</name>
    <desc>A 700m crag above Stickle Tarn, crossed by Jack&apos;s Rake — a rising Grade 1 scramble up the face of the cliff that is exposed, polished and unforgiving when wet. The summit is reached easily from behind if the Rake is not wanted. Detour: +4.7km, +271m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.459469" lon="-3.115148">
    <ele>709.0</ele>
    <name>Pike o’ Stickle 709m</name>
    <desc>A 709m rock thumb above Mickleden, with a neolithic axe factory in the scree below its summit. Detour: +4.3km, +266m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.457715" lon="-3.110473">
    <ele>682.0</ele>
    <name>Loft Crag 682m</name>
    <desc>A 682m Langdale Pike above Gimmer Crag. Detour: +4.8km, +271m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.470422" lon="-3.103210">
    <ele>736.0</ele>
    <name>Sergeant Man 736m</name>
    <desc>A 736m rocky knoll on the shoulder of High Raise, more distinct than its parent. Detour: +5.8km, +387m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.475729" lon="-3.112612">
    <ele>762.0</ele>
    <name>High Raise (Langdale) 762m</name>
    <desc>At 762m the geographical centre of the Lake District, a broad grassy dome with a wide view. Detour: +4.8km, +426m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.484219" lon="-3.165325">
    <ele>783.0</ele>
    <name>Glaramara 783m</name>
    <desc>A 783m ridge of rocky knolls and small tarns above Borrowdale. Detour: +17.1km, +898m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.492715" lon="-3.122337">
    <ele>574.0</ele>
    <name>Sergeant’s Crag 574m</name>
    <desc>A 574m crag above Langstrath, next to Eagle Crag. Detour: +8.0km, +510m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.499033" lon="-3.119422">
    <ele>521.0</ele>
    <name>Eagle Crag 521m</name>
    <desc>A 521m crag standing proud at the fork of Langstrath and Greenup — far more imposing than its height. Detour: +3.4km, +377m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.500144" lon="-3.096290">
    <ele>726.0</ele>
    <name>Ullscarf 726m</name>
    <desc>A 726m watershed fell between Borrowdale and Thirlmere; wet underfoot and quiet. Detour: +10.5km, +612m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.539293" lon="-3.139072">
    <ele>415.0</ele>
    <name>Grange Fell 415m</name>
    <desc>A 415m fell of wooded knolls in Borrowdale, with King&apos;s How as its finest top. Detour: +8.0km, +383m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.532783" lon="-3.162072">
    <ele>290.0</ele>
    <name>Castle Crag 290m</name>
    <desc>The only fell under 1000ft in the Wainwrights, at 290m. A quarried knoll in the Jaws of Borrowdale with a war memorial on top and a slate-spoil path. On the route.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.553269" lon="-3.181209">
    <ele>576.0</ele>
    <name>Maiden Moor 576m</name>
    <desc>A 576m top continuing the Cat Bells ridge southward. Detour: +10.1km, +624m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.535254" lon="-3.185325">
    <ele>653.0</ele>
    <name>High Spy 653m</name>
    <desc>A 653m fell along the crag edge above the Jaws of Borrowdale. Detour: +4.5km, +438m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.492887" lon="-3.197994">
    <ele>646.0</ele>
    <name>Base Brown 646m</name>
    <desc>A 646m fell above Seathwaite with a steep nose and the Hanging Stone. Detour: +9.4km, +720m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.526999" lon="-3.202083">
    <ele>753.0</ele>
    <name>Dale Head 753m</name>
    <desc>A 753m fell above Honister with a tall slate summit cairn and a fine view down Newlands. Detour: +5.2km, +490m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.502648" lon="-3.210634">
    <ele>697.0</ele>
    <name>Grey Knotts 697m</name>
    <desc>A 697m rocky top directly above Honister Pass. Detour: +1.8km, +141m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.496327" lon="-3.213535">
    <ele>715.0</ele>
    <name>Brandreth 715m</name>
    <desc>A 715m broad top on the Honister to Gable ridge. Detour: +3.4km, +185m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.516836" lon="-3.226469">
    <ele>648.0</ele>
    <name>Fleetwith Pike 648m</name>
    <desc>A 648m fell whose nose rises straight from Gatesgarth at the head of Buttermere. Steep, direct, and a superb viewpoint down the valley. Detour: +5.1km, +424m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.506763" lon="-3.247822">
    <ele>597.0</ele>
    <name>Haystacks 597m</name>
    <desc>At 597m, Wainwright&apos;s favourite fell and where his ashes were scattered. A knot of small tops, tarns and rock — far more interesting than its modest height suggests. Detour: +6.3km, +504m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.537673" lon="-3.213216">
    <ele>727.0</ele>
    <name>Hindscarth 727m</name>
    <desc>A 727m fell with a long northern ridge into the Newlands valley. Detour: +10.5km, +904m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.540134" lon="-3.236475">
    <ele>737.0</ele>
    <name>Robinson 737m</name>
    <desc>A 737m fell of rocky shelves at the western end of the Newlands ridge. Detour: +7.6km, +660m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.497423" lon="-3.281508">
    <ele>892.0</ele>
    <name>Pillar 892m</name>
    <desc>An 892m fell above Ennerdale, best known for Pillar Rock on its northern face — a true rock climb, not a walk. The summit itself is reached easily from Black Sail Pass. Detour: +13.5km, +1117m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.514641" lon="-3.268144">
    <ele>744.0</ele>
    <name>High Crag 744m</name>
    <desc>Detour: +4.4km, +632m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.521666" lon="-3.283812">
    <ele>807.0</ele>
    <name>High Stile 807m</name>
    <desc>The high point of the Buttermere ridge at 807m, looking straight down into the corrie above Bleaberry Tarn. Detour: +5.3km, +700m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.559564" lon="-3.269538">
    <ele>660.0</ele>
    <name>Whiteless Pike 660m</name>
    <desc>A 660m peaked top on the ridge above Crummock Water. Detour: +6.3km, +542m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.526891" lon="-3.299428">
    <ele>755.0</ele>
    <name>Red Pike (Buttermere) 755m</name>
    <desc>A 755m top of red syenite screes above Bleaberry Tarn. Detour: +4.8km, +651m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.529285" lon="-3.327320">
    <ele>633.0</ele>
    <name>Starling Dodd 633m</name>
    <desc>A 633m grassy top on the high ridge above Ennerdale. Detour: +7.9km, +544m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.534367" lon="-3.355304">
    <ele>616.0</ele>
    <name>Great Borne 616m</name>
    <desc>A 616m fell at the western end of the Ennerdale ridge. Detour: +10.7km, +560m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.552164" lon="-3.289409">
    <ele>355.0</ele>
    <name>Rannerdale Knotts 355m</name>
    <desc>A 355m rocky ridge above Crummock, famous for the bluebells that fill its valley in spring. Detour: +6.1km, +259m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.555356" lon="-3.320424">
    <ele>512.0</ele>
    <name>Mellbreak 512m</name>
    <desc>A 512m fell rising abruptly and independently from the shore of Crummock Water. Detour: +7.4km, +408m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.550677" lon="-3.343476">
    <ele>509.0</ele>
    <name>Hen Comb 509m</name>
    <desc>A 509m isolated fell reached across marshy ground near Loweswater. Detour: +9.8km, +430m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.563770" lon="-3.377933">
    <ele>573.0</ele>
    <name>Blake Fell 573m</name>
    <desc>A 573m high point of the Loweswater fells. Detour: +14.4km, +678m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.591192" lon="-3.337071">
    <ele>423.0</ele>
    <name>Low Fell 423m</name>
    <desc>A 423m fell with one of the best views of the Buttermere valley. Detour: +7.6km, +362m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.605481" lon="-3.345281">
    <ele>416.0</ele>
    <name>Fellbarrow 416m</name>
    <desc>A 416m grassy top on the north-western fringe. Detour: +11.3km, +441m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.571146" lon="-3.279180">
    <ele>852.0</ele>
    <name>Grasmoor 852m</name>
    <desc>At 852m the highest of the north-western fells, a broad whaleback above Crummock. Detour: +5.6km, +781m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.587334" lon="-3.278083">
    <ele>707.0</ele>
    <name>Whiteside 707m</name>
    <desc>Detour: +3.9km, +472m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.587513" lon="-3.261122">
    <ele>770.0</ele>
    <name>Hopegill Head 770m</name>
    <desc>A 770m summit at the head of Hobcarton Crag, one of the sharpest tops here. Detour: +3.1km, +270m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.571453" lon="-3.249798">
    <ele>839.0</ele>
    <name>Crag Hill 839m</name>
    <desc>An 839m hub of the Coledale fells with a trig point and steep drops north. Detour: +3.0km, +347m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.558040" lon="-3.243202">
    <ele>556.0</ele>
    <name>Knott Rigg 556m</name>
    <desc>A 556m ridge walk from the top of Newlands Hause, little visited. Detour: +8.2km, +683m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.571533" lon="-3.242066">
    <ele>773.0</ele>
    <name>Sail 773m</name>
    <desc>A 773m top reached by an engineered zigzag path on the Coledale ridge. Detour: +4.9km, +538m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.567183" lon="-3.228013">
    <ele>581.0</ele>
    <name>Ard Crags 581m</name>
    <desc>A 581m narrow grassy ridge above the Newlands valley. Detour: +5.0km, +543m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.576339" lon="-3.211271">
    <ele>637.0</ele>
    <name>Causey Pike 637m</name>
    <desc>A 637m fell with an unmistakable knobbly summit and a short scramble to reach it. Detour: +5.1km, +407m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.581621" lon="-3.222258">
    <ele>568.0</ele>
    <name>Outerside 568m</name>
    <desc>A 568m fell tucked below the Coledale ridge, usually bypassed. Detour: +3.1km, +275m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.591299" lon="-3.242668">
    <ele>791.0</ele>
    <name>Grisedale Pike 791m</name>
    <desc>A 791m fell with a sharp profile above Braithwaite and a long ridge approach. Detour: +7.1km, +527m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.585446" lon="-3.197532">
    <ele>455.0</ele>
    <name>Barrow 455m</name>
    <desc>Detour: +7.3km, +486m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.627333" lon="-3.234472">
    <ele>552.0</ele>
    <name>Lord’s Seat 552m</name>
    <desc>A 552m high point of the Whinlatter fells, among forestry. Detour: +10.1km, +526m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.629302" lon="-3.217492">
    <ele>468.0</ele>
    <name>Barf 468m</name>
    <desc>A 468m fell with a very steep scree face above Bassenthwaite. Detour: +8.7km, +443m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.642488" lon="-3.155902">
    <ele>746.0</ele>
    <name>Carl Side 746m</name>
    <desc>A 746m top on the Longside ridge approach to Skiddaw. Detour: +11.6km, +692m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.645080" lon="-3.166824">
    <ele>734.0</ele>
    <name>Long Side 734m</name>
    <desc>A 734m top on the finest ridge approach to Skiddaw. Detour: +13.1km, +762m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.635136" lon="-3.172736">
    <ele>502.0</ele>
    <name>Dodd 502m</name>
    <desc>A 502m forested cone below Skiddaw with a cleared summit viewpoint. Detour: +11.4km, +447m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.639969" lon="-3.137237">
    <ele>865.0</ele>
    <name>Skiddaw Little Man 865m</name>
    <desc>An 865m subsidiary top of Skiddaw with a better view than its parent. Detour: +14.6km, +831m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.633938" lon="-3.109182">
    <ele>715.0</ele>
    <name>Lonscale Fell 715m</name>
    <desc>A 715m eastern outlier of Skiddaw with an abrupt edge above the Glenderaterra. Detour: +12.0km, +684m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.612288" lon="-3.117884">
    <ele>368.0</ele>
    <name>Latrigg 368m</name>
    <desc>A 368m grassy hill directly above Keswick, with the best low-level view of Derwent Water and Borrowdale on the whole route. Detour: +5.4km, +283m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.568648" lon="-3.170826">
    <ele>451.0</ele>
    <name>Cat Bells 451m</name>
    <desc>A 451m ridge above Derwent Water, out of all proportion in popularity to its size — a short, rocky, thoroughly enjoyable up-and-down with a superb view over the lake. Detour: +12.9km, +365m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.552202" lon="-3.103870">
    <ele>608.0</ele>
    <name>High Seat 608m</name>
    <desc>A 608m top on notoriously wet ground on the Central Ridge. Detour: +9.0km, +527m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.565665" lon="-3.105781">
    <ele>590.0</ele>
    <name>Bleaberry Fell 590m</name>
    <desc>A 590m rocky top on the ridge above Keswick. Detour: +7.2km, +519m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.580812" lon="-3.120116">
    <ele>379.0</ele>
    <name>Walla Crag 379m</name>
    <desc>A 379m crag-edge above Derwent Water, minutes from the route. Detour: +3.4km, +304m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.639854" lon="-3.050464">
    <ele>868.0</ele>
    <name>Blencathra 868m</name>
    <desc>An 868m fell with a superb north-eastern approach by Sharp Edge — a narrow, genuinely exposed Grade 1 arete that has caused many accidents and should be avoided when wet or windy. Scales Fell gives a straightforward alternative both up and down. Detour: +13.0km, +961m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.593277" lon="-3.032240">
    <ele>726.0</ele>
    <name>Clough Head 726m</name>
    <desc>A 726m fell at the north end of the Dodds with a steep western face. Detour: +2.4km, +372m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.575411" lon="-3.019412">
    <ele>857.0</ele>
    <name>Great Dodd 857m</name>
    <desc>An 857m grassy dome at the northern end of the Helvellyn range. Detour: +9.2km, +464m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.555089" lon="-2.977156">
    <ele>675.0</ele>
    <name>Sheffield Pike 675m</name>
    <desc>A 675m fell between Glencoyne and Glenridding, above old lead workings. Detour: +1.9km, +125m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.561048" lon="-3.017507">
    <ele>843.0</ele>
    <name>Stybarrow Dodd 843m</name>
    <desc>An 843m grassy top on the northern Helvellyn ridge. Detour: +4.9km, +338m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.547570" lon="-3.017171">
    <ele>883.0</ele>
    <name>Raise 883m</name>
    <desc>An 883m fell holding the Lake District Ski Club tow on its northern slope. Detour: +5.8km, +426m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.541215" lon="-3.024742">
    <ele>863.0</ele>
    <name>White Side 863m</name>
    <desc>An 863m top on the main Helvellyn ridge, easily added. Detour: +7.0km, +399m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.526890" lon="-3.018202">
    <ele>950.0</ele>
    <name>Helvellyn 950m</name>
    <desc>At 950m, the most-climbed high fell in the district, with a summit shelter and trig point. Approaching by Striding Edge and leaving by Swirral Edge is the classic round: both are Grade 1 scrambles with real exposure, and neither is sensible in high wind, ice or poor visibility. Detour: +9.2km, +706m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.533258" lon="-3.009088">
    <ele>890.0</ele>
    <name>Catstye Cam 890m</name>
    <desc>A sharply conical 890m top just north of Helvellyn, often bypassed entirely despite being ten minutes off Swirral Edge. Detour: +7.2km, +643m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.518829" lon="-3.014912">
    <ele>891.0</ele>
    <name>Nethermost Pike 891m</name>
    <desc>An 891m top immediately south of Helvellyn with a fine eastern edge, usually ignored. Detour: +11.2km, +813m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.535246" lon="-2.985955">
    <ele>718.0</ele>
    <name>Birkhouse Moor 718m</name>
    <desc>A 718m shoulder crossed on the way to Striding Edge, with the Hole-in-the-Wall on it. Detour: +6.2km, +441m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.548936" lon="-2.960003">
    <ele>442.0</ele>
    <name>Glenridding Dodd 442m</name>
    <desc>A 442m small top above Glenridding with a good Ullswater view. Detour: +3.2km, +293m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.508971" lon="-3.011578">
    <ele>858.0</ele>
    <name>Dollywaggon Pike 858m</name>
    <desc>An 858m top at the southern end of the Helvellyn ridge above Grisedale Tarn. Detour: +13.1km, +655m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.511959" lon="-2.976126">
    <ele>841.0</ele>
    <name>St Sunday Crag 841m</name>
    <desc>An 841m fell with a long elegant ridge and the finest view of Helvellyn&apos;s eastern corries from across Grisedale. Detour: +7.8km, +683m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.544755" lon="-2.919713">
    <ele>657.0</ele>
    <name>Place Fell 657m</name>
    <desc>A 657m fell above Ullswater with a knobbly top and a superb lake view. Detour: +5.6km, +498m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.545009" lon="-2.885710">
    <ele>509.0</ele>
    <name>Beda Fell 509m</name>
    <desc>A 509m narrow ridge in Martindale, one of the quietest corners of the district. Detour: +8.4km, +437m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.525068" lon="-2.908455">
    <ele>567.0</ele>
    <name>Angletarn Pikes 567m</name>
    <desc>A 567m twin-topped fell beside Angle Tarn, one of the prettiest small tops here. Detour: +5.0km, +373m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.492178" lon="-2.977199">
    <ele>822.0</ele>
    <name>Hart Crag 822m</name>
    <desc>An 822m rocky top on the Fairfield horseshoe. Detour: +9.5km, +707m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.498986" lon="-2.910964">
    <ele>618.0</ele>
    <name>Hartsop Dodd 618m</name>
    <desc>A 618m steep-fronted top above Hartsop village. Detour: +3.1km, +455m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.497373" lon="-2.886224">
    <ele>699.0</ele>
    <name>Gray Crag 699m</name>
    <desc>A 699m long flat-topped ridge above Hayeswater. Detour: +4.9km, +487m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.515412" lon="-2.877346">
    <ele>696.0</ele>
    <name>Rest Dodd 696m</name>
    <desc>A 696m fell on the Martindale side of the High Street ridge. Detour: +1.6km, +159m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.513781" lon="-2.854141">
    <ele>802.0</ele>
    <name>High Raise (High Street) 802m</name>
    <desc>An 802m broad top, the highest of the far eastern fells after High Street. Detour: +3.0km, +144m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.507436" lon="-2.861731">
    <ele>792.0</ele>
    <name>Rampsgill Head 792m</name>
    <desc>A 792m top with crags falling into Rampsgill, beside Kidsty Pike. Detour: +1.2km, +73m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.506471" lon="-2.870977">
    <ele>739.0</ele>
    <name>The Knott 739m</name>
    <desc>A 739m rounded top at a junction of ridges above Hayeswater. On the route.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.505683" lon="-2.855517">
    <ele>780.0</ele>
    <name>Kidsty Pike 780m</name>
    <desc>A 780m top with a neat peaked profile above Riggindale, overlooking Haweswater. Detour: +2.2km, +86m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.493554" lon="-2.788876">
    <ele>655.0</ele>
    <name>Selside Pike 655m</name>
    <desc>A 655m fell on the eastern fringe, with a summit shelter. Detour: +15.8km, +814m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.482648" lon="-2.807188">
    <ele>713.0</ele>
    <name>Branstree 713m</name>
    <desc>A 713m grassy fell above Haweswater with survey pillars on its flank. Detour: +11.6km, +672m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.491239" lon="-2.864478">
    <ele>828.0</ele>
    <name>High Street 828m</name>
    <desc>An 828m whaleback carrying the line of a Roman road, with a wall along the top. Broad and easy going, and the route already crosses it. On the route.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.483229" lon="-2.853504">
    <ele>760.0</ele>
    <name>Mardale Ill Bell 760m</name>
    <desc>A 760m top between Nan Bield and High Street, above Blea Water. Detour: +3.3km, +109m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.476169" lon="-2.834838">
    <ele>778.0</ele>
    <name>Harter Fell (Mardale) 778m</name>
    <desc>A 778m fell above Nan Bield Pass, with a summit cairn built partly of old iron fence posts and a fine view down Haweswater. Detour: +6.8km, +363m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.482153" lon="-2.878177">
    <ele>784.0</ele>
    <name>Thornthwaite Crag 784m</name>
    <desc>A 784m top marked by a 4m stone beacon, at the junction of several ridges. Detour: +0.8km, +0m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.481994" lon="-2.899782">
    <ele>763.0</ele>
    <name>Stony Cove Pike 763m</name>
    <desc>A 763m top also known as Caudale Moor, above the Kirkstone Pass. Detour: +4.6km, +404m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.468708" lon="-2.873260">
    <ele>720.0</ele>
    <name>Froswick 720m</name>
    <desc>A 720m cone on the Kentmere horseshoe, a smaller echo of Ill Bell. Detour: +1.2km, +104m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.461530" lon="-2.871565">
    <ele>757.0</ele>
    <name>Ill Bell 757m</name>
    <desc>The finest top on the Kentmere horseshoe at 757m, cone-shaped with three large cairns. Detour: +4.5km, +355m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.470055" lon="-2.933467">
    <ele>776.0</ele>
    <name>Red Screes 776m</name>
    <desc>A 776m fell rising directly from the top of the Kirkstone Pass, with a summit tarn. Detour: +16.4km, +1254m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.452567" lon="-2.868290">
    <ele>706.0</ele>
    <name>Yoke 706m</name>
    <desc>A 706m fell with Rainsborrow Crag on its Kentmere flank. Detour: +9.6km, +648m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.428282" lon="-2.870859">
    <ele>516.0</ele>
    <name>Sallows 516m</name>
    <desc>A 516m grassy fell on the Kentmere fringe. Detour: +6.7km, +370m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.421004" lon="-2.883034">
    <ele>483.0</ele>
    <name>Sour Howes 483m</name>
    <desc>A 483m undulating fell above Troutbeck. Detour: +4.2km, +315m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.485064" lon="-2.967767">
    <ele>792.0</ele>
    <name>Dove Crag 792m</name>
    <desc>A 792m fell with a fine crag and the Priest&apos;s Hole cave beneath it. Detour: +10.1km, +689m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.437100" lon="-3.008264">
    <ele>335.0</ele>
    <name>Loughrigg Fell 335m</name>
    <desc>A 335m maze of little tops, tarns and caves between Grasmere and Ambleside — much more rambling than its height suggests. Detour: +4.9km, +345m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.465969" lon="-2.995088">
    <ele>612.0</ele>
    <name>Heron Pike 612m</name>
    <desc>A 612m top on the Rydal side of the Fairfield horseshoe. Detour: +6.1km, +522m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.494568" lon="-3.014311">
    <ele>736.0</ele>
    <name>Seat Sandal 736m</name>
    <desc>A 736m fell above Grisedale Tarn and Dunmail Raise. Detour: +9.7km, +691m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.496545" lon="-2.992743">
    <ele>873.0</ele>
    <name>Fairfield 873m</name>
    <desc>An 873m fell with a broad flat summit plateau that is confusing in cloud — the drops on the north side are abrupt. Detour: +11.5km, +856m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.484838" lon="-2.995547">
    <ele>766.0</ele>
    <name>Great Rigg 766m</name>
    <desc>A 766m top on the Fairfield horseshoe above Rydal. Detour: +8.8km, +696m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.450290" lon="-3.042519">
    <ele>395.0</ele>
    <name>Silver How 395m</name>
    <desc>A 395m top above Grasmere with a fine view of the vale and the Langdale Pikes. Detour: +2.2km, +213m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.460761" lon="-3.078267">
    <ele>541.0</ele>
    <name>Blea Rigg 541m</name>
    <desc>A 541m ridge of knolls between Easedale and Langdale. Detour: +8.5km, +480m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.432008" lon="-3.077512">
    <ele>469.0</ele>
    <name>Lingmoor Fell 469m</name>
    <desc>A 469m ridge between the two Langdales, with old slate quarries and a first-rate view of the Pikes. Detour: +6.2km, +368m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.405560" lon="-3.018275">
    <ele>323.0</ele>
    <name>Black Fell 323m</name>
    <desc>A 323m top with a National Trust monument column and a wide low-level view. Detour: +6.3km, +260m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.396243" lon="-3.056550">
    <ele>317.0</ele>
    <name>Holme Fell 317m</name>
    <desc>A 317m knot of rock and old quarries with a view down Yewdale. Detour: +3.7km, +167m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.400365" lon="-3.098248">
    <ele>762.0</ele>
    <name>Wetherlam 762m</name>
    <desc>A 762m fell riddled with old mine levels and shafts on its southern flanks — stay on the paths. Detour: +5.4km, +461m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.394761" lon="-3.121201">
    <ele>802.0</ele>
    <name>Swirl How 802m</name>
    <desc>An 802m hub of the Coniston fells, reached from Levers Hause or the Prison Band. Detour: +5.1km, +388m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.398312" lon="-3.125919">
    <ele>785.0</ele>
    <name>Great Carrs 785m</name>
    <desc>A 785m top with the wreckage of a wartime Halifax bomber on the col below its summit. Detour: +6.4km, +438m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.392762" lon="-3.142709">
    <ele>773.0</ele>
    <name>Grey Friar 773m</name>
    <desc>A 773m western outlier of the Coniston fells, looking over the Duddon. Detour: +7.0km, +414m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.376762" lon="-3.123790">
    <ele>796.0</ele>
    <name>Brim Fell 796m</name>
    <desc>A 796m grassy top on the ridge north of Coniston Old Man. Detour: +5.2km, +450m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.370486" lon="-3.122079">
    <ele>803.0</ele>
    <name>Coniston Old Man 803m</name>
    <desc>An 803m fell rising straight from the village, its flanks full of slate quarries and copper workings. Large summit cairn and a view to the sea. Detour: +5.0km, +507m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.370357" lon="-3.135929">
    <ele>778.0</ele>
    <name>Dow Crag 778m</name>
    <desc>A 778m summit perched above five great climbing buttresses dropping to Goats Water. The walk up is easy; the north face is not. Detour: +3.6km, +181m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.386757" lon="-3.205679">
    <ele>653.0</ele>
    <name>Harter Fell (Eskdale) 653m</name>
    <desc>A 653m fell of rocky tors above Eskdale, and one of the best-shaped small fells in the district. The true summit needs a short easy scramble. Detour: +2.9km, +400m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.422472" lon="-3.137370">
    <ele>701.0</ele>
    <name>Cold Pike 701m</name>
    <desc>A 701m top of three rocky summits beside the Crinkles. Detour: +12.1km, +992m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.410317" lon="-3.186340">
    <ele>549.0</ele>
    <name>Hard Knott 549m</name>
    <desc>A 549m rocky fell above the pass, with the remains of the Roman fort of Mediobogdum on its shoulder. Detour: +2.0km, +142m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.373898" lon="-3.233013">
    <ele>489.0</ele>
    <name>Green Crag 489m</name>
    <desc>A 489m rocky tor on the Eskdale moors, rarely visited. Detour: +6.3km, +456m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Muncaster Fell detour</name>
